mprehensive migration guides for v3 to v4 transition\nL192:   * Post Quantum: Implemented a NIST FIPS203 (ML-KEM) protocol on CUDA, fully open-source\nL193:   * Lattice Based Cryptography: Add support for Lattice based cryptography, with integer ring support and a full LaBRADOR prover (soon announced)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReleases · ingonyama-zk/icicle · GitHub (https://github.com/ingonyama-zk/icicle/releases)\nciteturn2view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/ingonyama-zk/icicle/releases\",\"pattern\":\"sumcheck\"}); Total lines: 877\nL318:   * Fix compilation for g++14.2.0 by 【121†@ChickenLover】 in 【156†#924】\nL319:   * [FEAT] add method to get challenges from sumcheck's Fiat-Shamir by 【127†@idanfr-ingo】 in 【157†#921】\nL320:   * Feat: balanced decomposition for Rq polynomials by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【158†#922】\nL321:   * Added Darkmode, Benchmarks update, fixed mobile display bug, added la… by 【90†@Shalmoni】 in 【159†#927】\nL322:   * fri final polynomial degree check by 【160†@krakhit】 in 【161†#928】\nL366:   * [FIX] Docs deployment by 【93†@jeremyfelder】 in 【167†#903】\nL373:   * [FEAT] Add ext field support to sumcheck by 【127†@idanfr-ingo】 in 【174†#917】\nL374:   * fix Merkle-Tree rust wrapper get_proof() for device-mem by 【88†@yshekel】 in 【175†#918】\nL527: ## Sorry, something went wrong.\nL528: \nL529: ### Uh oh!\nL530: \nL531: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL532: \nL533: ## No results found\nL534: \nL535: 【70†View all tags】\nL536: \nL537: 【83†Image: @github-actions†avatars.githubusercontent.com】 【84†github-actions】 released this 21 Apr 15:17\nL538: \nL539: 【215†v3.7.1】\nL540: \nL541: 【216†`65f9883`】\nL542: \nL543: # V3.7.1\nL544: \nL545: BUG FIX: Memory leak in Sumcheck-cuda\nL621:   * feat: FRI merkle tree API + CPU Backend by 【235†@ShanieWinitz】 in 【236†#795】\nL622:   * feat: balanced decomposition API b